This looks like the eye-tracking data set from the 2005 PASCAL challenge (Salojärvi et al.), where the task is to predict whether a word is relevant. Features such as lineNo, assgNo, titleNo and wordNo are position or identifier variables. Of these, wordNo and lineNo may carry some signal, while assgNo is probably weak. Fixation durations (firstfixDur, totalFixDur, meanFixDur) and the regression features are likely the most informative. Pupil diameter and the saccade-length features are likely to help only a little.

These scores are guesses from that background knowledge, not from the data.

